/Title (Scope: Scope refers to the region within the code where a certain variable is visible. Every function \(or class definition\) defines a scope within Python. Variables defined in this scope are called local variables. Variables that are available everywhere are called global variables. Scope rules allow you to use the same variable names in different functions without sharing values from one to the other.)
